what:
Half of 01455 (std shared across workspaces on one daemon); must land in the SAME batch as cargo's 01455 edits, which add `BuildConfig::std` and stop hashing the process env into std crates' unit identity.

(1) Build fix, 3 literal `BuildConfig { .. }` sites outside cargo's paths gain the new field after `library: ...,`:
- crates/blaze-engine/src/as_rustc/probe.rs:~128: `std: format!("{DIR}/std"),` (a check-only probe: nothing is placed there).
- crates/blaze-macro-eval/tests/corpus/load.rs:~166 and crates/hir-firewall/tests/real.rs:~213: `std: "/s/std".to_owned(),`.

(2) Soundness, hir-expand fn_macro.rs `get_env_inner`: the standard library's crates (`CrateOrigin::Lang`, set for `unit.is_std` units alone) see their crate env only, never the process env, as a std built elsewhere does. blaze-lower's `identity_of` no longer hashes the process env for Lang crates, so without this a std crate reading a process variable could reuse a stale record. Exact body:
```rust
fn get_env_inner(db: &Db, arg_id: MacroCallId, key: &Symbol) -> Option<String> {
    let krate = arg_id.loc(db).krate;
    db.env_is_read(krate, key.as_str());
    // As rustc reads them: what cargo set for the crate, then the process the build is for.
    // The standard library's crates read their own alone, as a std built elsewhere does: no
    // workspace's environment is in their identity.
    let own = krate.env(db).get(key.as_str());
    match krate.data(db).origin.is_lang() {
        true => own,
        false => own.or_else(|| base_db::process_env_var(db, key.as_str())),
    }
}
```
The library's sysroot crates read no process variable today (`env!`/`option_env!` of library/ outside docs and test-only crates are STD_ENV_ARCH and CARGO_*, all crate env), so no program changes.

(3) Consistency, optional: hir-def deps/reads.rs `Reads::values` hashes `process_env_var` of each name read; for a Lang crate it should hash none (what (2) makes it read). Today it over-keys std images, which is safe.
